#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
PLATOON (OBA Soft, 1987) - preservation port to Python
======================================================

This program executes a reconstructed, readable representation of the
MSX-BASIC logic recovered from PLATOONB.ASM and PLATOONC.ASM inside the
original disk image.

It is intentionally a text-mode preservation port. The original game uses
SCREEN 0 for the adventure itself, with INKEY$ single-key decisions.

Differences from the MSX version:
- input is blocking rather than busy-waiting INKEY$;
- original decision timeouts are disabled in this console port;
- LOCATE/COLOR/graphic border characters are simplified;
- the original title SCREEN 2 is supplied separately as PLATOON_title_screen.png;
- when the recovered part B reaches NEW, the port automatically starts part C;
- the disk image does not contain the additional part requested by the end of C,
  so the port ends there rather than inventing missing story content.

Controls:
- type the requested single letter and press Enter;
- Ctrl+C exits.
"""
